        <head>EXAMINER, FRIDAY, APRIL 14, 1899.</head>
        <p>THE EXAMINER, FRIDAY, APRIL 14, 1899.</p>
        <p>Alderman ROBERTS said ho thought new Offices were very necessary, but be booed the Gas Committee would not enter on a policy, which he understo )d had been abnnioned, of paying out of the profits after capital ex- penditure. If they would charge this arno ;sit on capi-al expenditure which they ought t-) do, he did not think there would be a dissentient voice about the grant,of the money. In answer to a question, The MAYOR said the offices were flr .managerial pur- poses, and no; for general secretarial worx. Councillor SHAW GREEN: At Lstigford. _</p>
