      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-04-14_WidnesExaminer_art0080" n="art0080">
        <head>[FOURTEEN PAGES, ON PENNYI</head>
        <p>[FOURTEEN PAGES, ON PENNYI</p>
        <p>my case was brain paralysis brought on by overwork and anxiety. A city friend r,uggested that I should try Dr. w!lliams' Pink Pills for Pale Pc9ple. I simply laughed, and thought nothing more of what I now re- gard a 3 a moat valuable suggestion. Mecting the same gentleman again, he asked me if the medicine was bene- ficial : on my replying that a purchase had not been made, he left me in the street, and appearing at this office later in the day, much to my amuitement placei before me twelve small pink-wrapped packages contain- ing Dr. Williams' Pink Plils,and insistud on my swallow- ing the first dose then and giving a promise tc take one pill after each meal. My friend is a penevering man : he caled the r following day, and the next, to know if I had ob?yed his injunction. When a man puts hand in pocket and buys for you when ill a medicine, the fact establishes at Inist beyond a doubt his belief in the efficacy</p>
        <p>of the prescription, and for this reason alone I deter- mined to finish the contents of the twelve boxes within a reasonable period. I consumed all, and always carry now in a silver match-box (filled twice a week) Dr. Wil- liams' Pink Pills. I take three a day, and am no longer troubled with locoingtor ataxy in the limbs, my brain is pertectly clear, and I work on an average from eight in the morning until eight at night, and I verily believe I sleep Ls soundly as if camping out on the South African veldt."</p>
        <p>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills are praised by all classes of people for the cure of paralysis, locomotor ataxy, rheu- matism and sciatica ; also all diseases arising from im- poverishment of the blcod,scrofula,rickets,consumption, atiemia, pale and sallow complexion. indigestion, loss of appetite, palpitation, nervous heathens and neuralgia, early decay, all fozms of Zemaks weakeess,and hysteria. These pills are a tonic., not a nurnative. They ame genuine only with the full notne. Dr.Williams' Pink Pills for Pale Peeple, and are sold by chemists, and by Dr. Williams' Medicino Company, 46, Holborn-viaduct. Lon- don, 8.C., at 2s. 9i. a box, or six boxes for 13s. 91. Pink pills sold loose or from glass jars are not Dr. Wil- liams' Pink Pills ; aetept them only in the pink closed wrapper as above described.</p>
