        <p>DRY, THIN, AND FALLING HAIR is due, in the majority of cases to imperfect action of the sebaceous or oil glands. Deplived of its proper nourishment, the heir becomes harsh and brittle, the scalp dry and scaly, and the roots choked and lifeless in a herd, dry skin. The purest, sweetest and most effective treatment is a warm shampol with CUTICURA SOAP, followed by light dro3mings with CIITICURA, purest of emollient skin cures, which will produce a clear, wholesome scalp and luxuri- ant, lustrous hair, when every other known method SPRING DRNSSES. W. T. WILLIAM 3 ;has just re- ceived the most Improved pro:illations in Gown and Coat:-and.Skirt Nisterials, Trinaminws. lor the coming season.—UNKEY-SrREIST, Warrington.</p>
