        <p>WHITEFIELD IAWN TENNIS CLUB.—The first annual meeting of the me'rine;s of the anove cub was he'd ar. rho house of Mr. J. W. Boachier, Whitefield-road, Mr.E. Eag!and occupying the char. The hoe. secr4ary and hon. treasurer submitted reports which were duly adopted. From thee r('ports it transpired that during the coarse of the pas', year, cot only had lawn tennis been freely indulged in, hut the members had had a picnic during the summer and a dance in the vi inter, both of which had been successful s)cially and finan- cially, and there we a with generally expr•ssei at thr• meeting that these two events should l be repeated triis year. Th. election of officers then took plac,, the fol- Viwing being appoint° I :--ffon secretary, Mr E Eog- -1 old ; hon. treasurer, Mr J W Bmichior ; captain, Mr M R Tomkinson who won the gentlemen's handicao) ; com- mittoe, Messrs J Do'an, W Skalton, and J Fhtcher ; and Mrs Caldwel, Mrs Tomkiuson, ani Miss II Balm- ford.</p>
